# Commit messages

Use one subject line:

```
type: imperative summary
```

Leave a space after the colon. Keep the summary short, specific, and in the imperative. Do not end it with a period.

| Prefix | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `feat:` | A new user-visible capability |
| `refact:` | A restructure that keeps behavior the same |
| `fix:` | A correction to broken behavior |
| `bug:` | A reported defect |
| `docs:` | Documentation only |
| `test:` | Tests only |
| `style:` | Formatting or visual polish without a logic change |
| `perf:` | A performance improvement |
| `chore:` | Tooling, config, or maintenance |

```
feat: add the Shabakat product panel
refact: extract product styles into product.css
fix: keep the logo mark visible in the light theme
bug: stop the contact form accepting a short message
```

Pick the prefix that matches the change. When a commit mixes types, use the prefix for the change a reviewer would notice first.
